.TH VAULT-RM 1 "September 2026" "vault" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vault-rm \- delete a stored file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vault rm
.RB [ \-\-key
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-\-vault
.IR DIR ]
.I NAME
.br
.B vault delete
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes the stored file \fINAME\fR from the vault. It does not ask for
confirmation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-key " PATH"
Key file. Default: $VAULT_KEY, else ~/.vault/key.
.TP
.BI \-\-vault " DIR"
Vault directory. Default: $VAULT_DIR, else ~/.vault/store.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VAULT_PASSPHRASE
Passphrase, instead of prompting on the terminal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vault (1),
.BR vault\-list (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Andy Dixon <vault@dixon.cx>, https://www.dixon.cx
